        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ZOBAH</strong> =Aram-Zobah, (Psalm 60, title), a Syrian province or kingdom to the south of Coele-Syria, and extending from the eastern slopes of Lebanon north and east toward the Euphrates. Saul and David had war with the kings of Zobah (1 Samuel 14:47; 2 Samuel 8:3; 10:6). <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
