        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>SCRIP</strong> a small bag or wallet usually fastened to the girdle (1 Samuel 17:40); “a shepherd’s bag.” In the New Testament it is the rendering of Gr. pera, which was a bag carried by travellers and shepherds, generally made of skin (Matthew 10:10; Mark 6:8; Luke 9:3; 10:4). The name “scrip” is meant to denote that the bag was intended to hold scraps, fragments, as if scraped off from larger articles, trifles. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
