        "in the name of Yahweh of Armies",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        """<strong>"Yahweh of Armies."</strong> <em>Yahweh tz’va’ot</em> — one of the Bible’s major divine titles, military and cosmic at once (the "armies" can be human armies, the celestial host, or both). David’s declaration inverts Goliath’s reliance on weaponry: "you come with sword and spear, I come in the name." The contrast is the chapter’s theological argument. The title <em>Yahweh tz’va’ot</em> appears 285 times in the OT, concentrated in Samuel-Kings and the prophets.""",
        "User original",
