        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>OFFENCE</strong> (1.) An injury or wrong done to one (1 Samuel 25:31; Romans 5:15). (2.) A stumbling-block or cause of temptation (Isaiah 8:14; Matthew 16:23; 18:7). Greek skandalon, properly that at which one stumbles or takes offence. The “offence of the cross” (Galatians 5:11) is the offence the Jews took at the teaching that salvation was by the crucified One, and by him alone. Salvation by the cross was a stumbling-block to their national pride. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
